IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`
IMPORT `sgba-sched`
IMPORT `sgba-p1-defs`
IMPORT `sgba-p5-apparatus`
IMPORT `sgba-p11-offences`
IMPORT `sgba-i-tvro-regs`
IMPORT `sgba-i-composition`
IMPORT `sgba-seat`
IMPORT `sgba-versions`

-- QUARANTINED (name starts sgba-tv-): THE SEAT LAYER FOR APPARATUS -- the questions of the person who owns a television or a satellite dish.
-- Nothing else may import this file. It IMPORTs layer 1 and the neutral seat helpers and restates no rule.
-- SEAT: a person in Singapore who owns a television or a satellite dish and asks "Do I need a Broadcasting Act licence?", "May I be granted one?", "Am I committing an offence?",
-- "What is the most I can be punished with?" and "What happens to the equipment?".
-- Dates. Questions 1 and 2 take TWO days, the day of the conduct and the day the law is read as at, and answer from the First Schedule versions of sgba-versions.l4: the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003),
-- the Revised Edition 2012 (31 August 2012), S 549/2012 (first published 31 October 2012, deemed in operation from 1 January 2011) and the consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- On a day before 31 July 2003, or a reading day after 4 November 2026 (the day the sources were last checked; assumed, not ruled), the answer is the not-covered sentence. A reading day from 2 October to 4 November 2026 is answered from the latest text deposited. On 4 November 2026 the orchestrating session searched the e-Gazette index (first page of each of two searches) and read the three results that name the Act; none amends a provision of the Broadcasting Act (detail in sgba-vintage.l4). That is what a first-page index search and three readings show; it is not a finding that nothing exists. The TVRO System Regulations as deposited are the text in force from 29 February 2004
-- to 4 November 2026; the Composition of Offences Regulations as deposited from 2 July 2007; for those the single day is the day of the conduct.
-- The KIND of equipment is a plain input (television, FM radio, AM radio, satellite dish).

§ `0. Helpers: the kind of equipment, and the answer for two days`

-- The person names the KIND of equipment in words; the facts a witness could state about each kind are the ones the First Schedule's definitions use.
-- A television set is used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service in monochrome or colour (and, being a set that receives sound, for aural reception too); a radio, FM or AM, for aural reception;
-- a satellite dish with its receiver is capable of direct reception from a satellite. The band of a radio (FM or AM) is not a fact any version of the First Schedule uses.
GIVEN `the kind of equipment` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Receiving equipment`
`the equipment of the kind the words name` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the kind of equipment` EQUALS "television" THEN JUST (`Receiving equipment` WITH `capable of the reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service in monochrome or colour` IS TRUE, `capable of direct reception of a broadcasting service from a satellite` IS FALSE)
           IF ^ EQUALS "FM radio" THEN JUST (`Receiving equipment` WITH `capable of the reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service in monochrome or colour` IS FALSE, `capable of direct reception of a broadcasting service from a satellite` IS FALSE)
           IF ^ EQUALS "AM radio" THEN JUST (`Receiving equipment` WITH `capable of the reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service in monochrome or colour` IS FALSE, `capable of direct reception of a broadcasting service from a satellite` IS FALSE)
           IF ^ EQUALS "satellite dish" THEN JUST (`Receiving equipment` WITH `capable of the reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service` IS FALSE, `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service in monochrome or colour` IS FALSE, `capable of direct reception of a broadcasting service from a satellite` IS TRUE)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN x IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`the answer for two days` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "The texts deposited do not say for those two days."
    WHEN JUST b THEN IF b THEN "Yes." ELSE "No."

`the kind of equipment is not on the list` MEANS "Say television, FM radio, AM radio or satellite dish: those are the kinds this question knows."

§ `1. Is my equipment broadcasting apparatus?`

-- Two days: the day of what you did or are doing (the conduct), and the day you read the law as at (what a reader could see on that day). The First Schedule was amended by S 549/2012, first published
-- on 31 October 2012 and deemed in operation from 1 January 2011, so for 2011 the answer depends on which of the two days comes first.
@export Is the equipment I have "broadcasting apparatus" under the Broadcasting Act, for what I did on one day, as the law was published on another day?
GIVEN `the kind of equipment` IS A STRING @desc One of: "television", "FM radio", "AM radio", "satellite dish" (a satellite dish with its receiver). Any other wording is a kind this question does not know.
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day you did, or are doing, what you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2011-06-01.
      `the day you read the law as at` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you read the law (the law as it could be read on that day), in ISO 8601 form, for example 2012-09-15.
GIVETH A STRING
`Is my equipment broadcasting apparatus, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the equipment of the kind the words name` `the kind of equipment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the kind of equipment is not on the list`
    WHEN JUST e THEN `the answer for two days` (`s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` `the day of the conduct` `the day you read the law as at` e)

-- The other reading of section 2(1) (fork F-BA-01 in NOTES.md): "specified in the First Schedule" qualifies only "designed or constructed for".
@export On the other reading of section 2(1), is the equipment I have "broadcasting apparatus", for what I did on one day, as the law was published on another day?
GIVEN `the kind of equipment` IS A STRING @desc One of: "television", "FM radio", "AM radio", "satellite dish" (a satellite dish with its receiver). Any other wording is a kind this question does not know.
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day you did, or are doing, what you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2011-06-01.
      `the day you read the law as at` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you read the law (the law as it could be read on that day), in ISO 8601 form, for example 2012-09-15.
GIVETH A STRING
`On the other reading, is my equipment broadcasting apparatus, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the equipment of the kind the words name` `the kind of equipment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the kind of equipment is not on the list`
    WHEN JUST e THEN `the answer for two days` (`s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading B` `the day of the conduct` `the day you read the law as at` e)

@export Which text of the First Schedule is read for what I did on one day, as the law was published on another day?
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day you did, or are doing, what you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2011-06-01.
      `the day you read the law as at` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you read the law, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2012-09-15.
GIVETH A STRING
`Which First Schedule is read for those two days?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the First Schedule version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` `the day of the conduct` `the day you read the law as at`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "The texts deposited do not say for those two days."
    WHEN JUST v THEN v's `source`

§ `2. Do I need a licence for what I do with it, and am I committing an offence?`

-- Fork F-BA-03 (NOTES.md): question 2 reads the premises phrase of s 20(1)(c) as qualifying both "operate" and "have" (reading A, the default). On that reading the three facts the noun holds collapse into the one input below: (operates OR has) AND the place is premises the person owns or occupies. The next question takes them separately.
@export Does section 20(1) of the Broadcasting Act require a licence for what I do with this equipment, and am I committing an offence under section 47 if I have none, for what I did on one day, as the law was published on another day?
GIVEN `the kind of equipment` IS A STRING @desc One of: "television", "FM radio", "AM radio", "satellite dish" (a satellite dish with its receiver). Any other wording is a kind this question does not know.
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day you did, or are doing, what you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2011-06-01.
      `the day you read the law as at` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you read the law (the law as it could be read on that day), in ISO 8601 form, for example 2012-09-15.
      `you install it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you install it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore.
      `you import it, offer it for sale, sell it, or hold it with a view to sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you import it, offer it for sale, sell it, or have it in your possession with a view to sale.
      `you operate it, or have it, on premises you own or occupy in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you operate it, or have it, on premises in Singapore that you own or occupy.
      `broadcasting services are received on or by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether broadcasting services are received on or by the equipment.
      `you act under and in accordance with a licence under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a broadcasting apparatus licence granted under section 20, and what you do is within its period and its terms and conditions.
      `you work it in the course of your duty as a member of the Singapore Armed Forces, the Police Force, the Vigilante Corps or the Civil Defence Force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work the equipment in the course of your duty as a member of the Singapore Armed Forces, the Singapore Police Force, the Vigilante Corps or the Singapore Civil Defence Force.
      `the Authority has exempted you, the equipment or its class under section 20(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has exempted you, the equipment, or the class of equipment from section 20(1).
      `a Ministerial order under section 60(b) exempts you` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has made an order in the Gazette under section 60(b) exempting you from section 20(1).
GIVETH A STRING
`Am I contravening section 20(1), which section 47 makes an offence, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the equipment of the kind the words name` `the kind of equipment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the kind of equipment is not on the list`
    WHEN JUST e THEN `the answer for two days` (`s 47 the person is guilty of an offence` (`s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` `the day of the conduct` `the day you read the law as at` e (`Dealing with apparatus` WITH `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore` IS `you install it`, `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale` IS `you import it, offer it for sale, sell it, or hold it with a view to sale`, `operates it` IS `you operate it, or have it, on premises you own or occupy in Singapore`, `has it` IS FALSE, `the place is premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person` IS `you operate it, or have it, on premises you own or occupy in Singapore`, `broadcasting services are received on or by it` IS `broadcasting services are received on or by it`) `you act under and in accordance with a licence under section 20` `you work it in the course of your duty as a member of the Singapore Armed Forces, the Police Force, the Vigilante Corps or the Civil Defence Force` `the Authority has exempted you, the equipment or its class under section 20(4)` `a Ministerial order under section 60(b) exempts you`))

-- Fork F-BA-03 (NOTES.md): does "on any premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person" in s 20(1)(c) qualify "operate" as well as "have"? Question 2 reads it as qualifying both (the default); this question reads it as qualifying only "have".
-- It keeps the default reading of the First Schedule (F-BA-01).
@export On the other reading of the premises phrase in section 20(1)(c) (that it qualifies only "have", so that "operate" is not confined to my own premises), am I committing an offence under section 47 if I have no licence, for what I did on one day, as the law was published on another day?
GIVEN `the kind of equipment` IS A STRING @desc One of: "television", "FM radio", "AM radio", "satellite dish" (a satellite dish with its receiver). Any other wording is a kind this question does not know.
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day you did, or are doing, what you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2011-06-01.
      `the day you read the law as at` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you read the law (the law as it could be read on that day), in ISO 8601 form, for example 2012-09-15.
      `you install it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you install it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore.
      `you import it, offer it for sale, sell it, or hold it with a view to sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you import it, offer it for sale, sell it, or have it in your possession with a view to sale.
      `you operate it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you operate the equipment, at the place you ask about.
      `you have it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have the equipment at the place you ask about.
      `the place is premises in Singapore that you own or occupy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place where you operate it or have it is premises in Singapore that you own or occupy.
      `broadcasting services are received on or by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether broadcasting services are received on or by the equipment.
      `you act under and in accordance with a licence under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a broadcasting apparatus licence granted under section 20, and what you do is within its period and its terms and conditions.
      `you work it in the course of your duty as a member of the Singapore Armed Forces, the Police Force, the Vigilante Corps or the Civil Defence Force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work the equipment in the course of your duty as a member of the Singapore Armed Forces, the Singapore Police Force, the Vigilante Corps or the Singapore Civil Defence Force.
      `the Authority has exempted you, the equipment or its class under section 20(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has exempted you, the equipment, or the class of equipment from section 20(1).
      `a Ministerial order under section 60(b) exempts you` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has made an order in the Gazette under section 60(b) exempting you from section 20(1).
GIVETH A STRING
`If the premises phrase qualifies only "have", am I contravening section 20(1), which section 47 makes an offence, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the equipment of the kind the words name` `the kind of equipment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the kind of equipment is not on the list`
    WHEN JUST e THEN `the answer for two days` (`s 47 the person is guilty of an offence` (`s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A, reading B of F-BA-03` `the day of the conduct` `the day you read the law as at` e (`Dealing with apparatus` WITH `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore` IS `you install it`, `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale` IS `you import it, offer it for sale, sell it, or hold it with a view to sale`, `operates it` IS `you operate it`, `has it` IS `you have it`, `the place is premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person` IS `the place is premises in Singapore that you own or occupy`, `broadcasting services are received on or by it` IS `broadcasting services are received on or by it`) `you act under and in accordance with a licence under section 20` `you work it in the course of your duty as a member of the Singapore Armed Forces, the Police Force, the Vigilante Corps or the Civil Defence Force` `the Authority has exempted you, the equipment or its class under section 20(4)` `a Ministerial order under section 60(b) exempts you`))

§ `3. May I be granted a licence for a satellite receiving system?`

-- The institution-only rule (regulation 3(2)) is printed whole in S 354/2001, in operation from 1 August 2001, and in the Revised Edition 2004 in the same words (sgba-versions.l4). Before 1 August 2001 the text of regulation 3 was not obtained.
@export Under the Broadcasting (TVRO System) Regulations, may I be granted a licence to install or operate a TVRO system (a satellite receiving system), for what I do on one day?
GIVEN `the day you ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2025-03-15.
      `you are a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate (for example a company, a partnership or an association), and not an individual acting on your own.
      `you are an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you are is an undertaking within the meaning of the Regulations (the definition of "institution" says it includes any undertaking).
GIVETH A STRING
`May I be granted a TVRO licence under regulation 3(2)?` MEANS
    `the answer to a yes or no question` (`TVRO reg 3(2) the person may be granted a licence, from 1 August 2001, for conduct on a day` `the day you ask about` `you are a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` `you are an undertaking`)

§ `3A. Did the television and radio licensing regulations say I needed a licence?`

-- The Broadcasting (Television and Radio Licensing) Regulations (Rg 1): the Revised Edition 2004 (29 February 2004), as amended from 21 June 2004 by S 333/2004, and revoked by S 548/2012, published on 31 October 2012 and deemed in operation from 1 January 2011.
-- Two days: the day of what you did and the day you read the law as at. The question asks what THE REGULATIONS say, not whether a licence was needed by law: section 20(1) of the Act is the question of sections 1 and 2 above. No text of the Regulations before 29 February 2004 was obtained.
GIVEN v IS A `Rg 1 version`
      `the kind of equipment` IS A STRING
      `where the equipment is` IS A STRING
      `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is temporary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Rg 1 text read says a licence is needed under the version` MEANS
    IF `the use is temporary` AND `Rg 1 reg 24 and 29 a licence is not required for the temporary use of a receiver, under the version` v `the use is temporary` `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE BRANCH IF `the kind of equipment` EQUALS "television" AND `where the equipment is` EQUALS "at home or in other ordinary premises" THEN `Rg 1 reg 27(1) the person contravenes the prohibition on operating a broadcast television receiver without a licence, under the version` v TRUE FALSE
                IF `the kind of equipment` EQUALS "television" AND `where the equipment is` EQUALS "in a car or other road vehicle" THEN `Rg 1 reg 28(2) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver, under the version` v TRUE FALSE `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act`
                IF `the kind of equipment` EQUALS "television" AND `where the equipment is` EQUALS "on a boat, ship or aircraft" THEN `Rg 1 reg 28(2) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver, under the version` v FALSE TRUE `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act`
                IF `the kind of equipment` EQUALS "television" AND `where the equipment is` EQUALS "in a shop, office or other commercial property" THEN (`Rg 1 reg 27(1) the person contravenes the prohibition on operating a broadcast television receiver without a licence, under the version` v TRUE FALSE) OR `Rg 1 reg 29A(1) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver, under the version` v TRUE
                IF (`the kind of equipment` EQUALS "FM radio" OR `the kind of equipment` EQUALS "AM radio") AND `where the equipment is` EQUALS "in a car or other road vehicle" THEN `Rg 1 reg 23 states in terms that a licence is required for the broadcast sound receiver, under the version` v TRUE FALSE `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act`
                IF (`the kind of equipment` EQUALS "FM radio" OR `the kind of equipment` EQUALS "AM radio") AND `where the equipment is` EQUALS "on a boat, ship or aircraft" THEN `Rg 1 reg 23 states in terms that a licence is required for the broadcast sound receiver, under the version` v FALSE TRUE `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act`
                OTHERWISE `Rg 1 reg 23 states in terms that a licence is required for the broadcast sound receiver, under the version` v FALSE FALSE FALSE

`the kind or place is not on the list` MEANS "Say television, FM radio or AM radio for the kind, and one of: at home or in other ordinary premises; in a car or other road vehicle; on a boat, ship or aircraft; in a shop, office or other commercial property."

GIVEN `the kind of equipment` IS A STRING
      `where the equipment is` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind and place are ones this question knows` MEANS
    (`the kind of equipment` EQUALS "television" OR `the kind of equipment` EQUALS "FM radio" OR `the kind of equipment` EQUALS "AM radio") AND (`where the equipment is` EQUALS "at home or in other ordinary premises" OR `where the equipment is` EQUALS "in a car or other road vehicle" OR `where the equipment is` EQUALS "on a boat, ship or aircraft" OR `where the equipment is` EQUALS "in a shop, office or other commercial property")

@export Do the Broadcasting (Television and Radio Licensing) Regulations, as they could be read on one day, say that I needed a licence for this equipment where I had it, for what I did on another day?
GIVEN `the kind of equipment` IS A STRING @desc One of: "television", "FM radio", "AM radio". Any other wording is a kind this question does not know.
      `where the equipment is` IS A STRING @desc One of: "at home or in other ordinary premises", "in a car or other road vehicle", "on a boat, ship or aircraft", "in a shop, office or other commercial property".
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day you did, or are doing, what you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2009-06-01.
      `the day you read the law as at` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you read the law (the law as it could be read on that day), in ISO 8601 form, for example 2012-09-15.
      `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vessel has a ship station licence under the Telecommunications Act (relevant only on a boat, ship or aircraft).
      `the use is temporary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you use the equipment only temporarily.
      `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes.
GIVETH A STRING
`Did the Television and Radio Licensing Regulations say I needed a licence, for that conduct, with the law read as at that day?` MEANS
    IF `the kind and place are ones this question knows` `the kind of equipment` `where the equipment is`
    THEN CONSIDER `the Rg 1 version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` `the day of the conduct` `the day you read the law as at`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN "The texts deposited do not say for those two days."
         WHEN JUST v THEN `the plain yes or no` (`the Rg 1 text read says a licence is needed under the version` v `the kind of equipment` `where the equipment is` `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act` `the use is temporary` `the use is in a public place, or at an official or social function, or at a function organised for charitable purposes`)
    ELSE `the kind or place is not on the list`

@export Which text of the Television and Radio Licensing Regulations is read for what I did on one day, as the law was published on another day?
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day you did, or are doing, what you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2009-06-01.
      `the day you read the law as at` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which you read the law, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2012-09-15.
GIVETH A STRING
`Which Television and Radio Licensing Regulations text is read for those two days?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Rg 1 version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` `the day of the conduct` `the day you read the law as at`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "The texts deposited do not say for those two days."
    WHEN JUST v THEN v's `source`

§ `4. What can happen to me and to the equipment?`

@export If I am convicted of contravening section 20(1), what is the most I can be punished with, and what happens to the equipment?
GIVETH A STRING
`What is the most I can be punished with under section 47?` MEANS
    `the punishment in words` `s 47 the punishment on conviction`

@export Can the Authority compound the offence, instead of my being prosecuted, and for how much?
GIVEN `the day you ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2025-03-15.
      `the section of the Broadcasting Act the offence is under` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of the section that makes the act an offence, for example 47.
      `the sum the Authority would collect` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum, in dollars, the Authority would collect from you in place of prosecution.
GIVETH A STRING
`May the Authority compound this offence for that sum?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 2 the offence may be compounded by the Authority in accordance with section 57(1), on` `the day you ask about` `the section of the Broadcasting Act the offence is under`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "The Act, as deposited, does not say for that date."
    WHEN JUST prescribed THEN `the plain yes or no` (`s 57(1) the Authority may compound the offence by collecting that sum` prescribed `the sum the Authority would collect`)

@export If an officer finds my apparatus, may it be seized, and when is it deemed forfeited if I am not prosecuted?
GIVEN `the person who found it is a police officer or an employee the Authority authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who found the apparatus is a police officer or an employee the Authority authorised.
      `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that broadcasting apparatus used is not licensed by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the officer has reasonable grounds for believing the broadcasting apparatus in use is not licensed by the Authority.
GIVETH A STRING
`May the officer enter and inspect my premises and seize it?` MEANS
    `the plain yes or no` (`s 51(1) the person may enter and inspect the premises and seize broadcasting apparatus found there which appears to be used for or in connection with broadcasting` `the person who found it is a police officer or an employee the Authority authorised` FALSE FALSE `the officer has reasonable grounds for believing that broadcasting apparatus used is not licensed by the Authority`)

@export If my apparatus was seized and I am not prosecuted, is it deemed forfeited to the Authority?
GIVEN `no prosecution is brought for the apparatus seized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no prosecution is brought with regard to the apparatus seized.
      `you made a claim within 2 months from the date of seizure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a claim to the apparatus was made within 2 months from the date of seizure.
GIVETH A STRING
`Is my seized apparatus deemed forfeited to the Authority?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 51(2) the apparatus is taken and deemed to be forfeited to the Authority` `no prosecution is brought for the apparatus seized` `you made a claim within 2 months from the date of seizure`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "Section 51(2) does not say on those facts."
    WHEN JUST b THEN `the plain yes or no` b
